load @term/seed/code/algebra/exterior
  find exterior-algebra

# A bivector: a grade-two element of an exterior or geometric algebra, an oriented area, the wedge of two vectors. A
# bivector is the natural object of rotation: it names a plane and a rate of turning, and exponentiating it gives a
# rotor. The bivectors of a space are its infinitesimal rotations, the Lie algebra of its rotation group. The form
# carries the exterior algebra the bivector lives in.
form bivector
  link algebra, like exterior-algebra
